#: ../../library/turtle.rst:3
msgid ":mod:`!turtle` --- Turtle graphics"
msgstr ":mod:`!turtle` --- Turtle-Grafik"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:10
msgid "**Source code:** :source:`Lib/turtle.py`"
msgstr "**Quellcode:** :source:`Lib/turtle.py`"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:28
msgid ""
"Turtle can draw intricate shapes using programs that repeat simple moves."
msgstr ""
"Turtle kann komplizierte Formen zeichnen, indem es Programme verwendet, die "
"einfache Bewegungen wiederholen."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:34
msgid ""
"Imagine a robotic turtle starting at (0, 0) in the x-y plane. After an "
"``import turtle``, give it the command ``turtle.forward(15)``, and it moves "
"(on-screen!) 15 pixels in the direction it is facing, drawing a line as it "
"moves. Give it the command ``turtle.right(25)``, and it rotates in-place 25 "
"degrees clockwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:40
msgid ""
"Turtle graphics is an implementation of `the drawing tools introduced in "
"Logo <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turtle_(robot)>`_ in 1967. It was "
"created as an educational tool, and its instant, visible feedback makes it "
"an effective way for learners to encounter programming concepts. It is also "
"a convenient way to produce simple graphical output without bringing in "
"external libraries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:46
msgid "This document includes four main sections:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:48
msgid ":ref:`turtle-tutorial` teaches the basics of turtle drawing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:49
msgid ""
":ref:`turtle-reference` describes the functions, methods and classes this "
"module defines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:51
msgid ":ref:`turtle-howtos` details how to handle specific tasks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:52
msgid ""
":ref:`turtle-explanation` provides background on the object-oriented "
"interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:57
msgid ""
"Turtle graphics requires the :mod:`tkinter` :term:`optional module`. The "
"python.org installers for Windows and macOS include it, but some Linux "
"distributions and other platforms may package it separately. If ``import "
"turtle`` fails with an error mentioning ``_tkinter``, look for documentation "
"from your distributor (that is, whoever provided Python to you). Check this "
"in advance if you're planning to use turtle graphics with a learner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:70
msgid "Tutorial"
msgstr "Tutorial"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:72
msgid ""
"New users should start here. In this tutorial we'll explore some of the "
"basics of turtle drawing."
msgstr ""
"Neue Benutzer sollten hier beginnen. In diesem Tutorial erkunden wir einige "
"der Grundlagen des Turtle-Zeichnens."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:77
msgid "Starting a turtle environment"
msgstr "Eine Turtle-Umgebung starten"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:79
msgid "In a Python shell, import all the objects of the ``turtle`` module::"
msgstr "Importiere in einer Python-Shell alle Objekte des Moduls ``turtle``::"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:81
msgid "from turtle import *"
msgstr "from turtle import *"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:83
msgid ""
"If you run into a ``No module named '_tkinter'`` error, you'll have to "
"install the :mod:`Tk interface package <tkinter>` on your system."
msgstr ""
"Falls du auf einen Fehler ``No module named '_tkinter'`` stößt, musst du "
"das :mod:`Tk-Interface-Paket <tkinter>` auf deinem System installieren."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:88
msgid "Basic drawing"
msgstr "Einfaches Zeichnen"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:90
msgid "Send the turtle forward 100 steps::"
msgstr "Schicke die Turtle 100 Schritte vorwärts::"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:92
msgid "forward(100)"
msgstr "forward(100)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:94
msgid ""
"You should see (most likely, in a new window on your display) a line drawn "
"by the turtle, heading East. Change the direction of the turtle, so that it "
"turns 120 degrees left (anti-clockwise)::"
msgstr ""
"Du solltest (höchstwahrscheinlich in einem neuen Fenster auf deinem "
"Bildschirm) eine von der Turtle gezeichnete Linie sehen, die nach Osten "
"zeigt. Ändere die Richtung der Turtle, sodass sie sich um 120 Grad nach "
"links dreht (gegen den Uhrzeigersinn)::"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:98
msgid "left(120)"
msgstr "left(120)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:100
msgid "Let's continue by drawing a triangle::"
