#: ../../library/turtle.rst:470
msgid ""
"Move the turtle forward by the specified *distance*, in the direction the "
"turtle is headed."
msgstr ""
"Bewege die Turtle um die angegebene *distance* vorwärts, in die Richtung, in "
"die die Turtle blickt."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:473
msgid ""
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(0.00,0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.forward(25)\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(25.00,0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.forward(-75)\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(-50.00,0.00)"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(0.00,0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.forward(25)\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(25.00,0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.forward(-75)\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(-50.00,0.00)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:490 ../../library/turtle.rst:733
#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1005 ../../library/turtle.rst:1549
msgid "a number"
msgstr "eine Zahl"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:492
msgid ""
"Move the turtle backward by *distance*, opposite to the direction the turtle "
"is headed.  Do not change the turtle's heading."
msgstr ""
"Bewege die Turtle um *distance* rückwärts, entgegen der Richtung, in die die "
"Turtle blickt. Die Ausrichtung der Turtle wird dabei nicht verändert."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:501
msgid ""
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(0.00,0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.backward(30)\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(-30.00,0.00)"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(0.00,0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.backward(30)\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(-30.00,0.00)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:516
msgid ""
"Turn turtle right by *angle* units.  (Units are by default degrees, but can "
"be set via the :func:`degrees` and :func:`radians` functions.)  Angle "
"orientation depends on the turtle mode, see :func:`mode`."
msgstr ""
"Drehe die Turtle um *angle* Einheiten nach rechts. (Die Einheit ist "
"standardmäßig Grad, kann aber über die Funktionen :func:`degrees` und :func:"
"`radians` festgelegt werden.) Die Winkelausrichtung hängt vom Turtle-Modus "
"ab, siehe :func:`mode`."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:526
msgid ""
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"22.0\n"
">>> turtle.right(45)\n"
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"337.0"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"22.0\n"
">>> turtle.right(45)\n"
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"337.0"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:541
msgid ""
"Turn turtle left by *angle* units.  (Units are by default degrees, but can "
"be set via the :func:`degrees` and :func:`radians` functions.)  Angle "
"orientation depends on the turtle mode, see :func:`mode`."
msgstr ""
"Drehe die Turtle um *angle* Einheiten nach links. (Die Einheit ist "
"standardmäßig Grad, kann aber über die Funktionen :func:`degrees` und :func:"
"`radians` festgelegt werden.) Die Winkelausrichtung hängt vom Turtle-Modus "
"ab, siehe :func:`mode`."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:551
msgid ""
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"22.0\n"
">>> turtle.left(45)\n"
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"67.0"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"22.0\n"
">>> turtle.left(45)\n"
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"67.0"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:565
msgid "a number or a pair/vector of numbers"
msgstr "eine Zahl oder ein Paar/Vektor von Zahlen"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:566 ../../library/turtle.rst:599
#: ../../library/turtle.rst:600
msgid "a number or ``None``"
msgstr "eine Zahl oder ``None``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:568
msgid ""
"If *y* is ``None``, *x* must be a pair of coordinates or a :class:`Vec2D` (e."
"g. as returned by :func:`pos`)."
msgstr ""
"Wenn *y* ``None`` ist, muss *x* ein Koordinatenpaar oder ein :class:`Vec2D` "
"sein (z. B. wie von :func:`pos` zurückgegeben)."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:571
msgid ""
"Move turtle to an absolute position.  If the pen is down, draw line.  Do not "
"change the turtle's orientation."
msgstr ""
"Bewege die Turtle zu einer absoluten Position. Wenn der Stift unten ist, "
"zeichne eine Linie. Die Ausrichtung der Turtle wird dabei nicht verändert."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:580
msgid ""
">>> tp = turtle.pos()\n"
">>> tp\n"
"(0.00,0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.setpos(60,30)\n"
">>> turtle.pos()\n"
"(60.00,30.00)\n"
">>> turtle.setpos((20,80))\n"
">>> turtle.pos()\n"
"(20.00,80.00)\n"
">>> turtle.setpos(tp)\n"
">>> turtle.pos()\n"
"(0.00,0.00)"
msgstr ""
">>> tp = turtle.pos()\n"
">>> tp\n"
"(0.00,0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.setpos(60,30)\n"
">>> turtle.pos()\n"
"(60.00,30.00)\n"
">>> turtle.setpos((20,80))\n"
">>> turtle.pos()\n"
"(20.00,80.00)\n"
">>> turtle.setpos(tp)\n"
">>> turtle.pos()\n"
"(0.00,0.00)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:601
msgid "a boolean"
msgstr "Ein Boolean"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:603
msgid ""
"Move turtle to an absolute position. Unlike goto(x, y), a line will not be "
"drawn. The turtle's orientation does not change. If currently filling, the "
"polygon(s) teleported from will be filled after leaving, and filling will "
"begin again after teleporting. This can be disabled with fill_gap=True, "
"which makes the imaginary line traveled during teleporting act as a fill "
"barrier like in goto(x, y)."
msgstr ""
"Bewege die Turtle zu einer absoluten Position. Im Gegensatz zu goto(x, y) "
"wird dabei keine Linie gezeichnet. Die Ausrichtung der Turtle ändert sich "
"nicht. Falls gerade gefüllt wird, wird das Polygon, von dem aus teleportiert "
"wurde, nach dem Verlassen gefüllt, und das Füllen beginnt nach dem "
"Teleportieren erneut. Dies kann mit fill_gap=True deaktiviert werden, "
"wodurch die gedachte Linie, die während des Teleportierens zurückgelegt "
"wird, wie bei goto(x, y) als Füllbarriere wirkt."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:616
msgid ""
">>> tp = turtle.pos()\n"
">>> tp\n"
"(0.00,0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.teleport(60)\n"
">>> turtle.pos()\n"
"(60.00,0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.teleport(y=10)\n"
">>> turtle.pos()\n"
"(60.00,10.00)\n"
">>> turtle.teleport(20, 30)\n"
">>> turtle.pos()\n"
"(20.00,30.00)"
msgstr ""
">>> tp = turtle.pos()\n"
">>> tp\n"
"(0.00,0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.teleport(60)\n"
">>> turtle.pos()\n"
"(60.00,0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.teleport(y=10)\n"
">>> turtle.pos()\n"
"(60.00,10.00)\n"
">>> turtle.teleport(20, 30)\n"
">>> turtle.pos()\n"
"(20.00,30.00)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:639
msgid ""
"Set the turtle's first coordinate to *x*, leave second coordinate unchanged."
msgstr ""
"Setze die erste Koordinate der Turtle auf *x*, die zweite Koordinate bleibt "
"unverändert."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:648
msgid ""
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(0.00,240.00)\n"
">>> turtle.setx(10)\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(10.00,240.00)"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(0.00,240.00)\n"
">>> turtle.setx(10)\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(10.00,240.00)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:662
msgid ""
"Set the turtle's second coordinate to *y*, leave first coordinate unchanged."
msgstr ""
"Setze die zweite Koordinate der Turtle auf *y*, die erste Koordinate bleibt "
"unverändert."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:670
msgid ""
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(0.00,40.00)\n"
">>> turtle.sety(-10)\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(0.00,-10.00)"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(0.00,40.00)\n"
">>> turtle.sety(-10)\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(0.00,-10.00)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:685
msgid ""
"Set the orientation of the turtle to *to_angle*.  Here are some common "
"directions in degrees:"
msgstr ""
"Setze die Ausrichtung der Turtle auf *to_angle*. Hier sind einige gängige "
"Richtungen in Grad:"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:689
msgid "standard mode"
msgstr "Standardmodus"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:689
